{
  "abstract": "Global query standardization and module weighting over summed projected ($d_{\\mathrm{proj}}=16$) negative log-odds (`NLO`) gradients raised CATT `Rule Routings` (`RR`, seed 1001) Recall@10 to `42.83%` on held-out test facts, yet still trailed lexical `BM25` (`99.80%`) by over 55 points. We identify the underlying algebraic bottleneck: summing 496 heterogeneous LoRA modules *before* coordinate-wise query Z-scoring (`Z-Agg`) and top-$k$ pooling allows noisy middle-layer modules (`L12-L22`) and inter-module variance to dilute discriminative tokens prior to selection. Reversing this order inside CATT's exact all-token $d_{\\mathrm{proj}}=16$ NLO tensor—applying non-transductive `Z-Agg` and sparse top-$k$ pooling independently within each module before weighted aggregation (`Per-Module Z-Agg Weighted`, $k=3$)—raises held-out Test-15 Recall@10 on `RR` from `42.83%` to `87.50%` (`95% CI [82.67%, 92.33%]`, `AUC = 0.9955`, `MRR = 99.17%`; `80.45%` across all 50 facts), retaining `86.67%` under a strict 250-doc train-only InfoNCE denominator and `91.17%` when excluding all reference-category candidates. Every held-out test category reaches $\\ge 70.0\\%$ R@10 (`lamp`: `7.5%` to `77.5%`). Mechanistic probes show early `Band 1 (L2-11)` (`case_cond` `45.5%`) is causally essential (`50.0%` B/A when zeroed) whereas late `Band 2 (L23-30)` (`rule_clause` `33.9%`) retains `96.67%` B/A; `1,500`-doc twin audits stay below parity (`AUC_mem = 0.4156`, persisting under $\\epsilon=0$ and RMS normalization) vs. own-loss `1.0000`; untrained `B=0` controls remain low on `RR` (`12.67%`) while hitting `99.25%` (`Per-Layer`) on `FB-distr` via repeated answer tokens; and pre-pooling `Token-Z` rescues CATT's `.ce` `FB-distr` pool (`4.35%` to `64.05%`).",
